Reason:
The introduction of the `else` branch incorrectly modified the logic such that the clearing of `PWM_EN` and `PWM_CLK_GATING` bits would never execute, leading to these bits remaining set when the PWM was supposed to be disabled. This caused backlight issues on boards using the Allwinner A20 SoC.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (state->enabled)
    ctrl |= BIT_CH(PWM_EN, pwm->hwpwm);
```
Reason:
By removing the `else` branch, the code now only sets `PWM_EN` when the PWM is enabled, while the clearing of `PWM_EN` and `PWM_CLK_GATING` bits is handled later in the function. This restores the previous behavior and ensures that the bits are cleared appropriately when the PWM is disabled, resolving the backlight issues.

